<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('/partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>

<%- include('/partials/header') %>

<section class="page-hero faq">
  <div class="copy">
    <h1>Before you <em>visit</em>.</h1>
    <div class="jp-line">よくあるご質問　—　FAQ</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="wrap">

    <!-- Group 1: Visiting basics -->
    <div class="faq-group">
      <div class="label">
        <span class="num">I — Basics</span>
        <h3>Visiting the temple</h3>
        <span class="jp">参拝について</span>
      </div>
      <div class="qs faq-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">01</span>
            <span class="q-text">Can non-Buddhists and foreign visitors enter the temple?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Yes — all are welcome during open hours (9:00 — 17:00), regardless of background or belief. No reservation is needed, and there is no admission fee. You are welcome to walk the grounds, sit quietly in the main hall, or simply pass through on your way up the hillside.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">02</span>
            <span class="q-text">Do I need to pay to enter?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>No. Entry to the grounds and the main hall is free. A small offering box (<em>saisen-bako</em>) sits in front of the altar if you wish to give — a coin of any denomination is fine.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">03</span>
            <span class="q-text">How long does a visit usually take?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>As Myohokkein is a relatively small temple,
            a full visit usually takes around 15 minutes. Although guided tours in English are not available,
            visitors are always welcome to stop by and explore at their own pace.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">04</span>
            <span class="q-text">Can I reach the temple on foot from Shin-Kobe Station?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>No. We recommend taking the train from Shin-Kobe Station
            to Shinkaichi Station instead. The temple is just a one-minute walk
            from the West Exit of Shinkaichi Station.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Group 2: Etiquette -->
    <div class="faq-group">
      <div class="label">
        <span class="num">II — Etiquette</span>
        <h3>Inside the hall</h3>
        <span class="jp">作法・マナー</span>
      </div>
      <div class="qs faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">05</span>
            <span class="q-text">Is there etiquette I should follow inside the hall?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Nothing strict. Speak softly, keep phones on silent, and feel free to place your palms together (<em>gasshō</em>) before the altar if you wish.</p>
            <p>You do not need to chant, bow, or follow any particular form. Sitting quietly is itself a kind of practice.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">06</span>
            <span class="q-text">Can I take photographs?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Photography is welcome throughout the grounds. Inside the main hall please refrain from using flash, and avoid photographing worshippers or ceremonies in progress. If a service is underway, it is best to wait until it is over.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">07</span>
            <span class="q-text">Is there a dress code?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>No formal dress code. Casual clothing is fine.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Group 3: Accessibility & support -->
    <div class="faq-group">
      <div class="label">
        <span class="num">III — Practical</span>
        <h3>Accessibility &amp; support</h3>
        <span class="jp">アクセシビリティ・対応</span>
      </div>
      <div class="qs faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">08</span>
            <span class="q-text">Are there English-speaking guides or materials?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Some staff in the temple office may be able to assist in simple English,
            though this is not always available. If you would like a more detailed introduction to the temple,
            we kindly ask that you contact us by email in advance.<br>
            As there are currently no English information boards on the grounds,
            we recommend exploring the temple while referring to this website.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">09</span>
            <span class="q-text">Is there a café or a place to sit?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>A small restaurant, “Sekai,” is located within the temple grounds
            and is currently open by reservation only.
            Seating can be found throughout the temple,
            providing places to pause and rest during your visit.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Group 4: Faith & ceremonies -->
    <div class="faq-group">
      <div class="label">
        <span class="num">IV — Practice</span>
        <h3>Faith &amp; ceremonies</h3>
        <span class="jp">信仰・法要</span>
      </div>
      <div class="qs faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">10</span>
            <span class="q-text">What is Nichiren-shū? How is it different from other Buddhist schools?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Nichiren-shū is one of the major schools of Japanese Buddhism, founded in the 13th century by Nichiren Shōnin. Its practice centres on the Lotus Sūtra and the chanted phrase <em>Namu Myōhō Renge Kyō</em>.</p>
            <p>Read more on our <a href="<%= rootPath %>about/">About</a> page.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">11</span>
            <span class="q-text">Can I attend a ceremony or memorial service?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Most regular services are open to quiet observation — there is no need to register. As foreign visitors are still relatively uncommon at the temple,
we would appreciate it if you could contact us in advance. Monthly observances and major annual ceremonies are also streamed on our <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCNAaxCyBY_0nOeElQppw3AQ/live?app=desktop" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube channel</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">12</span>
            <span class="q-text">I'd like to request a memorial or prayer service. Is that possible?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Yes — we accept requests for memorial services (<em>hōyō</em>), prayer rites (<em>kitō</em>), ancestor and, Animal Memorial Services offerings from anyone, regardless of denomination or nationality. If you contact us in advance,
we will be happy to discuss the details with you.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span class="q-num">13</span>
            <span class="q-text">Can I bring children?</span>
            <span class="q-plus"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="q-body">
            <p>Of course. Children are welcome on the grounds and in the main hall. The koi garden in particular is a favourite — a quiet space to walk and watch the fish.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- contact strip -->
    <div class="contact-strip">
      <div>
        <h3>Still have a <em>question</em>?</h3>
        <p>If you cannot find the answer here, please feel free to send us a message on Instagram.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info">
        <div class="row"><span>Telephone</span><strong>078-575-2608</strong></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Office hours</span><strong>09:00 — 17:00</strong></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Open daily</span><strong>07:00 — 17:00</strong></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Instagram</span><strong><a href="https://www.instagram.com/explore/locations/236870120051032/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"> @myohokkein</a></strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<%- include('/partials/footer') %>

<script src="<%= rootPath %>site.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
